# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — AICTE CaseSync
## Integrated Institution Complaint Monitoring and Cross-Bureau Coordination Platform | SIH Working Prototype

### 1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Improve the existing AICTE CaseSync website and transform it into a professional, responsive, genuinely interactive working prototype for the Smart India Hackathon.

The project addresses the following problem:

AICTE receives complaints and grievances concerning technical education institutions from students, faculty members, stakeholders, and other concerned parties. These cases may be handled independently by the Regulation Bureau (RB), Public Grievance Redressal Cell (PGRC), Regional Offices, and other concerned Bureaus/Cells.

Without a centralized institution-wise view, different Bureaus/Cells may act on complaints concerning the same institution without sufficient visibility into each other's activities. This can lead to duplicate work, delayed disposal, overlapping actions, and difficulty identifying the responsible Bureau or officer.

Build a single-window platform that gives authorized officials a consolidated, institution-centric view of complaints, assignments, actions, transfers, escalations, deadlines, and potential overlaps.

**The main product is an integrated institution complaint monitoring system, not a standalone ML classification application.**

Do not make a large “AI Classification” section the center of the homepage or dashboard. ML must operate as an integrated backend capability supporting institution identification, related-case matching, and overlap detection. The primary interface must focus on institutions, complaints, Bureau/Cell coordination, actionable alerts, and case status.

Preserve the existing website where useful, but correct its weak alignments, inconsistent spacing, nonfunctional controls, incomplete workflows, and visual inconsistencies.

Do not replace the existing product with a generic template or start from a blank dashboard unless necessary.

